# OpenSSH configuration of the piano developer mode, read by `sshd -i` in
# piano-devmode-ssh@.service.  piano-devmode-ssh.socket decides where it
# listens; ListenAddress and Port have no effect in this mode.
# Host keys are the system's /etc/ssh/ssh_host_*_key; `piano-devmode check`
# creates missing ones (ssh-keygen -A) on every start.
# sshd keeps the first value it reads for a keyword: the lines below take
# precedence over the administrator's drop-ins included at the end, which can
# still tighten the rest, e.g. "PasswordAuthentication no" once a key is in
# ~/.ssh/authorized_keys.  Password logins otherwise follow the sshd default
# through PAM, i.e. local accounts with a password.
PermitRootLogin no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
UsePAM yes
PrintMotd no
AcceptEnv LANG LC_* COLORTERM NO_COLOR
Subsystem sftp internal-sftp
Include /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/*.conf
